<header><div class="brand">Stratic Market</div><h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
<div class="meta">Effective 2 November 2026 &middot; Estimated reading time 20 minutes</div></header>
<main>
<details class="toc" open><summary>Contents</summary><ol><li><a href="#s1"><span>01</span>Introduction</a></li><li><a href="#s2"><span>02</span>Who this Policy applies to</a></li><li><a href="#s3"><span>03</span>Information you give us</a></li><li><a href="#s4"><span>04</span>Information we collect automatically</a></li><li><a href="#s5"><span>05</span>How we use information</a></li><li><a href="#s6"><span>06</span>Who can see what</a></li><li><a href="#s7"><span>07</span>Sharing with other parties</a></li><li><a href="#s8"><span>08</span>Payments</a></li><li><a href="#s9"><span>09</span>Orders and delivery</a></li><li><a href="#s10"><span>10</span>Listing rules and prohibited items</a></li><li><a href="#s11"><span>11</span>Chat and messages</a></li><li><a href="#s12"><span>12</span>Photos and images</a></li><li><a href="#s13"><span>13</span>Dashboards, statistics and your shop link</a></li><li><a href="#s14"><span>14</span>Security</a></li><li><a href="#s15"><span>15</span>How long we keep information</a></li><li><a href="#s16"><span>16</span>Your choices and rights</a></li><li><a href="#s17"><span>17</span>Children</a></li><li><a href="#s18"><span>18</span>International use and transfers</a></li><li><a href="#s19"><span>19</span>Fees</a></li><li><a href="#s20"><span>20</span>Changes to this Policy</a></li><li><a href="#s21"><span>21</span>How to use Stratic Market: complete walk-through</a></li><li><a href="#s22"><span>22</span>Frequently asked questions</a></li><li><a href="#s23"><span>23</span>Contact us</a></li></ol></details>
<section id="s1"><div class="num">01</div><h2>Introduction</h2><p>Stratic Market (&ldquo;Stratic Market&rdquo;, &ldquo;we&rdquo;, &ldquo;us&rdquo;, &ldquo;our&rdquo;) is an online marketplace where people can list products, find products, chat with each other, and place orders. This Privacy Policy explains what information the Stratic Market app and website (together, the &ldquo;Service&rdquo;) collect, why we collect it, who can see it, how long we keep it, and what choices you have. It also explains, in plain steps, how to use each part of the Service, because many of the choices described here are made by using those features.</p><p>By creating an account, listing a product, placing an order, sending a message, or otherwise using the Service, you agree to the practices described in this Policy. If you do not agree, please do not use the Service. This Policy is long on purpose: we would rather describe each feature in detail than hide anything in a single sentence. You can use the contents list at the top to jump to the part you need, and the small gold links inside the text open the matching screen of the app so that you can act immediately.</p><p>Throughout this Policy, a &ldquo;buyer&rdquo; is a person who browses or orders products, a &ldquo;seller&rdquo; is a person who lists products or runs a shop on the Service, and one person can be both. &ldquo;Content&rdquo; means anything you put on the Service, such as photos, product details, messages and profile information.</p></section>
<section id="s2"><div class="num">02</div><h2>Who this Policy applies to</h2><p>This Policy applies to everyone who uses the Service: visitors who only browse, signed-in buyers, and sellers. Some sections apply only to sellers (for example, payment QR codes and payment gateways) and some only to buyers (for example, checkout). Where a section applies to only one group we say so at the start of that section.</p><p>The Service may contain links to pages that are not operated by us, such as a seller&rsquo;s own social-media page that they choose to share. We do not control those pages and this Policy does not apply to them.</p></section>
<section id="s3"><div class="num">03</div><h2>Information you give us</h2><p><b>Account information.</b> When you create an account we ask for your name, email address, mobile number (with country code), country and preferred language. If you choose to sign in with Google, Google gives us your name and email address; we never see your Google password. You can add or change a profile photo and your display name at any time from <a class="dl" href="/shop#go-editprofile">Edit profile &amp; photo</a>.</p><p><b>Seller and shop information.</b> When you <a class="dl" href="/shop#go-sell">list a product</a> you provide product photos (up to twelve), a product name, price, an optional maximum retail price (MRP), a category, a description, an optional expiry date, your name or shop name, mobile number, full shop address, city, district and the currency of the price. This information is shown to buyers so that they can evaluate the product and contact you.</p><p><b>Payment QR code.</b> If you want buyers to pay you directly, you upload your own scannable UPI or payment QR for that product. We check that the image is a genuine scannable QR code and reject ordinary photos. The QR is private to that product: it is shown only to a buyer who chooses online payment for that product, and to nobody else.</p><p><b>Payment gateway keys.</b> Larger sellers can <a class="dl" href="/shop#go-gateway">connect a payment gateway</a> (Razorpay) by entering their own Key ID and Key Secret. We confirm with the gateway that the keys are valid before saving them. The Key Secret is stored in encrypted form, is never shown back to you or to any buyer, and is used only by our server to create and verify payments for your orders.</p><p><b>Order information.</b> When you place an order we collect your name, mobile number, delivery address, city, state, country, the products and quantities, the payment method you choose, and for QR payments the Transaction ID you type in. The seller of the product receives the delivery details needed to deliver your order.</p><p><b>Messages and photos in chat.</b> If you use <a class="dl" href="/shop#go-chat">Chat</a>, we store the messages you send, any photos you send (with optional captions), the time each message was sent, and its status (sent, delivered, seen, edited or deleted). Videos cannot be sent.</p><p><b>Things you tell us when you contact us.</b> If you use Help, the AI Assistant, or report or block another user, we receive what you write and the identity of the account involved.</p></section>
<section id="s4"><div class="num">04</div><h2>Information we collect automatically</h2><p><b>Views and likes.</b> To show sellers honest numbers, we count how many different people viewed a product and how many liked it. To count a person only once, the app keeps a small random identifier on your device. If you are signed in when you view a product, the seller can see that your account viewed it, together with your display name and profile photo, in the viewer list on the seller&rsquo;s own shop page. If you are not signed in, you are counted but not named.</p><p><b>Technical information.</b> Like most online services, our servers receive your IP address, browser or app type and the pages or actions requested. We use this to keep the Service running, to limit abuse (for example, too many messages or login attempts in a short time), and to investigate security problems.</p><p><b>Cookies and similar technologies.</b> We use a session cookie to keep you signed in, a security token to protect forms and actions from being triggered by other websites, and the device identifier described above. We use your language and appearance choices (such as chat theme, sound and text size) stored on your own device so the app looks the way you left it.</p><p><b>Typing signals.</b> When you type in a chat, a short signal is sent so the other person can see that you are typing. These signals are not stored.</p></section>
<section id="s5"><div class="num">05</div><h2>How we use information</h2><p>We use the information described above to: create and secure your account; show your products to buyers and show buyers&rsquo; orders to sellers; let buyers and sellers talk to each other; process and verify payments and confirm orders only when a payment has genuinely been received; show you accurate statistics on your <a class="dl" href="/shop#go-dashboard">Product Dashboard</a> and <a class="dl" href="/shop#go-advdash">Advanced Dashboard</a>; send service messages such as order notifications; detect and prevent fraud, fake listings and abuse; enforce our rules, including the rule against expired products; and improve and maintain the Service.</p><p>We do not sell your personal information. We do not use the content of your private chats for advertising. The Service does not currently show third-party advertisements.</p></section>
<section id="s6"><div class="num">06</div><h2>Who can see what</h2><p>The table of visibility below describes the main kinds of information and who can see each of them. &ldquo;Operators&rdquo; means the authorised people who run Stratic Market and who need access to keep the Service safe and to resolve problems.</p><p><b>Your product listings</b> &mdash; visible to anyone who uses the Service or opens your shop link. This includes the product photos, name, price, description, your shop name, city and the contact details you entered on the listing.</p><p><b>Your shop page</b> &mdash; the public part (shop name and products) is visible to anyone with the link. The statistics, the advanced dashboard and the list of people who viewed your products are visible only to you when you are signed in as the owner.</p><p><b>Your payment QR</b> &mdash; visible only to a buyer who chooses online payment for that product, and to operators when verifying a payment dispute.</p><p><b>Your gateway Key Secret</b> &mdash; visible to nobody. It cannot be read back out of the app.</p><p><b>Your delivery details on an order</b> &mdash; visible to you, to the seller of that order, and to operators.</p><p><b>Your chat</b> &mdash; visible to the two people in that conversation. Operators may look at a conversation only when it is reported or when needed to investigate abuse or a security issue.</p><p><b>Your profile name and photo</b> &mdash; visible to people you chat with and, if you are signed in when you view a seller&rsquo;s product, to that seller in their viewer list.</p></section>
<section id="s7"><div class="num">07</div><h2>Sharing with other parties</h2><p>We share information only in the following situations. First, with the other side of a transaction, as described above: sellers get what they need to fulfil an order and buyers get what they need to contact and trust a seller. Second, with service providers that help us run the Service, such as the companies that host our servers and database, and, for orders paid through a seller&rsquo;s gateway, the payment gateway (Razorpay) that processes the payment. These providers may process information only to provide their service to us or to the seller. Third, when required by law or to protect the rights, safety and property of our users, the public or Stratic Market. Fourth, with your consent, for example when you choose to send a picture of your dashboard to someone in chat.</p><p>If Stratic Market is ever merged with or acquired by another business, information may be transferred as part of that transaction, and we will keep protecting it under terms no less protective than this Policy.</p></section>
<section id="s8"><div class="num">08</div><h2>Payments</h2><p><b>Cash on Delivery.</b> You pay the seller in cash when the product is delivered. Nothing is paid inside the app.</p><p><b>Seller&rsquo;s QR.</b> You see the seller&rsquo;s QR after choosing online payment, pay the exact full amount using your own payment app, and enter the Transaction ID. Stratic Market does not receive this money; it goes directly from you to the seller. The seller (or an operator) then checks that the amount received is at least the order total before the order is confirmed. If the amount received is lower than the order total, even by one rupee, the order is not confirmed.</p><p><b>Gateway payment.</b> For sellers who have connected a gateway, you can pay by UPI, card or net banking in a secure window provided by the gateway. We never see or store your card number or banking password. Your order is confirmed only after our server verifies the payment with the gateway, and only if the amount paid is at least the order total. If a payment fails or is abandoned, the order is not confirmed.</p><p><b>Never share secrets.</b> Stratic Market and genuine sellers will never ask for your OTP, PIN, password or card details in chat. Pay only through the QR on the product page or the secure payment option in the app. If anyone asks for these, stop and use the report option in the chat menu.</p></section>
<section id="s9"><div class="num">09</div><h2>Orders and delivery</h2><p>Delivery is the responsibility of the seller. At present, the seller delivers the product personally and bears the delivery cost. Once Stratic Market has been installed on your phone for six months, Stratic Market will bear the delivery cost. We may change this arrangement in future, and any change will be shown here before it takes effect.</p><p>Buyers can follow their orders from <a class="dl" href="/shop#go-orders">My orders</a>. Sellers see the orders for their products, including the delivery details they need, in <a class="dl" href="/shop#go-delivery">Seller orders</a> and in the <a class="dl" href="/shop#go-dashboard">Product Dashboard</a>. A seller should mark and fulfil orders promptly. A buyer should provide a correct address and a reachable mobile number.</p></section>
<section id="s10"><div class="num">10</div><h2>Listing rules and prohibited items</h2><p><b>Expired products are not allowed.</b> You must never list a product whose expiry date has passed. Expired items are rejected. Listing them can lead to action against your account and, where the law requires, to legal proceedings. If a product has an expiry date, you must enter the correct date when you <a class="dl" href="/shop#go-sell">list it</a>. Entering a false date is also a breach of these rules.</p><p>You must not list products that are illegal to sell, counterfeit, stolen, unsafe, or that you do not have the right to sell. You must not upload a payment QR that does not belong to you, and you must not use the Service to take money without delivering the product. Photos must show the product you are actually selling. We may remove listings and suspend or close accounts that break these rules.</p></section>
<section id="s11"><div class="num">11</div><h2>Chat and messages</h2><p><a class="dl" href="/shop#go-chat">Chat</a> lets a buyer and a seller talk about a product. Messages are stored so that you can see the conversation again later on any device where you are signed in. Each message of yours shows one tick when it has been sent, two grey ticks when it has reached the other person&rsquo;s app, and two green ticks when the other person has opened the chat and seen it.</p><p>You can send photos using the plus (+) button, choosing from your gallery or taking a new photo. The photo first opens in a preview so you can add a caption, and only then is it sent. Photos are reduced in size before sending. Tapping any photo opens it full screen and lets you save it to your gallery. Anyone you send a photo to can save it, so send only what you are happy for them to keep.</p><p>You can press and hold one of your own messages to edit it (within fifteen minutes of sending, for text messages), copy it, or delete it for everyone. Deleting for everyone removes the content from the other person&rsquo;s chat as well; a grey notice that a message was deleted remains until you remove that notice too, which you can do by pressing and holding it. The &ldquo;Select messages&rdquo; option lets you tick many messages and delete them together. You can only delete or edit your own messages, never the other person&rsquo;s.</p><p>From the three-dot menu in a chat you can change the chat theme, switch the message sound on or off, change the text size, search the chat, see all photos in the chat, export the chat as a text file to your device, and block or report the other person. These display choices are stored on your device and are not visible to the other person.</p><p>Please be polite. Harassment, threats, hate, sexual content, scams and attempts to move a buyer to an unsafe payment method are not allowed. We may act on reports and may review a reported conversation.</p></section>
<section id="s12"><div class="num">12</div><h2>Photos and images</h2><p>Product photos you upload are shown on your listing. If you switch on &ldquo;Auto white background&rdquo; the app processes the photo on your device to give it a clean white background before uploading. Only upload photos you have the right to use. Do not upload photos that show other people&rsquo;s private information, documents, or anything you would not want strangers to see.</p><p>Profile photos are small square pictures shown beside your name. You can replace your profile photo at any time from <a class="dl" href="/shop#go-editprofile">Edit profile &amp; photo</a>.</p></section>
<section id="s13"><div class="num">13</div><h2>Dashboards, statistics and your shop link</h2><p>The <a class="dl" href="/shop#go-dashboard">Product Dashboard</a> shows the sales, likes and buyer locations for your products. The <a class="dl" href="/shop#go-advdash">Advanced Dashboard</a> contains forty cards covering orders, payments, countries, currencies, views, likes and more. Each card has a three-dot control that lets you switch between the last 24 hours, the last 7 days and the last 30 days. All figures come from real activity on your own products. Where there is nothing to count the card says so rather than showing an invented number. You can send a picture of your dashboard to someone in chat.</p><p>Your <a class="dl" href="/shop#go-shoplink">shop link</a> is a web address for your shop. When you tap the button the link is copied so that you can paste it in WhatsApp, Instagram or any browser. Anyone with the link can see your shop and products. When you open your own link while signed in you also see your private numbers and the list of signed-in people who viewed your products.</p></section>
<section id="s14"><div class="num">14</div><h2>Security</h2><p>We protect information with a number of measures, including encrypted connections (HTTPS), encryption of payment gateway secrets, verification of payment signatures on our server rather than trusting the app, protection of actions against cross-site requests, limits on how fast messages and logins can be attempted, and restrictions on who can open private chat photos. Payment QR codes and gateway secrets are never included in pages that other users can see.</p><p>No online service can promise perfect security. You also have a part to play: keep your password private, sign out on shared phones, and never share OTPs. If you think someone else has used your account, change your password and contact us through Help straight away.</p></section>
<section id="s15"><div class="num">15</div><h2>How long we keep information</h2><p>We keep your account and content for as long as your account is active, so that your listings, orders and chats remain available to you. When you delete a message or photo for everyone, we remove its content from our systems and from the other person&rsquo;s view. We may keep limited records of orders and payments for as long as needed to resolve disputes, prevent fraud, keep accounts, and comply with the law. If you ask us to close your account, we will delete or anonymise your personal information, except what we must keep for those purposes.</p></section>
<section id="s16"><div class="num">16</div><h2>Your choices and rights</h2><p>You can: update your name and photo in <a class="dl" href="/shop#go-editprofile">Edit profile &amp; photo</a>; edit or remove your listings from <a class="dl" href="/shop#go-products">My products</a>; review your orders in <a class="dl" href="/shop#go-orders">My orders</a>; delete your own chat messages and photos as described above; export a chat; change your language in <a class="dl" href="/shop#go-language">Language</a>; disconnect a payment gateway from <a class="dl" href="/shop#go-gateway">Payment gateway</a>; and sign out from Profile. To ask for a copy of your information, to correct it, or to close your account and delete your information, use <a class="dl" href="/shop#go-help">Help</a> or the <a class="dl" href="/shop#go-ai">AI Assistant</a>, and we will respond.</p><p>You may also clear the data stored on your own device (for example, theme choices and the cart) by clearing the app&rsquo;s storage in your phone settings.</p></section>
<section id="s17"><div class="num">17</div><h2>Children</h2><p>The Service is not directed to children, and sellers should be adults who can lawfully run a business and receive payments. If you believe a child has given us personal information without a parent&rsquo;s permission, tell us through Help and we will take steps to remove it.</p></section>
<section id="s18"><div class="num">18</div><h2>International use and transfers</h2><p>Stratic Market lets people list products and place orders across countries and currencies. Our servers and service providers may be located in a country different from yours, so your information may be processed and stored outside your country. We take steps to keep it protected wherever it is handled. Local laws on sales, taxes, customs and consumer rights still apply to your transactions, and you are responsible for following them.</p></section>
<section id="s19"><div class="num">19</div><h2>Fees</h2><p>Stratic Market currently takes no commission on sales made through the Service. Sellers receive buyers&rsquo; payments directly, by cash, by their own QR, or through their own gateway account. A gateway provider may charge the seller its own fees; those are between the seller and the provider. If we ever introduce fees, we will say so here and in the app before they apply.</p></section>
<section id="s20"><div class="num">20</div><h2>Changes to this Policy</h2><p>We may update this Policy from time to time, for example when we add a feature or when the law changes. The updated version will appear on this page with a new effective date at the top. If a change is significant, we will also tell you in the app. Using the Service after a change means you accept the updated Policy.</p></section>
<section id="s21"><div class="num">21</div><h2>How to use Stratic Market: complete walk-through</h2><p><b>1. Create your account.</b> Open the app and choose <a class="dl" href="/shop#go-signup">Create account</a>, or <a class="dl" href="/shop#go-login">Sign in</a> if you already have one. Tap <a class="dl" href="/shop#go-profile">Profile</a> (bottom right) to see your account screen.</p><p><b>2. List a product.</b> Tap the golden plus (+) button in the middle of the bottom bar, or open <a class="dl" href="/shop#go-sell">Sell a product</a>. Add photos with Camera or Gallery, up to twelve. Keep &ldquo;Auto white background&rdquo; on for clean pictures.</p><p><b>3. Upload your payment QR.</b> On the same page, in the &ldquo;Seller payment QR&rdquo; box, tap Choose File and select your own scannable UPI QR. Only a real scannable QR is accepted.</p><p><b>4. Large sellers: connect a gateway.</b> Right below the QR box is &ldquo;Large seller? Connect Payment Gateway&rdquo;, or open <a class="dl" href="/shop#go-gateway">Payment gateway</a>. Enter your Razorpay Key ID and Key Secret. After this, buyers can also pay by UPI, card or net banking.</p><p><b>5. Finish the listing.</b> Enter the product name, price, optional MRP, category, description, the expiry date if the product has one, your shop name, mobile number, address, city, district and currency. Then tap Post product.</p><p><b>6. Browse and buy.</b> Use <a class="dl" href="/shop#go-categories">Categories</a>, the search bar or the home page. Open a product to see its photos and details, like it, add it to your <a class="dl" href="/shop#go-cart">Cart</a>, or buy it directly. At checkout enter your name, mobile and address, then choose Cash on Delivery, the seller&rsquo;s QR, or secure gateway payment if the seller offers it.</p><p><b>7. Follow orders.</b> Buyers open <a class="dl" href="/shop#go-orders">My orders</a>. Sellers open <a class="dl" href="/shop#go-sellerorders">Seller orders</a> to see what they must deliver.</p><p><b>8. Chat.</b> Open <a class="dl" href="/shop#go-chat">Chat</a> from a product or from the menu. Type and send. Use the plus button for photos. Press and hold your own message for Edit, Copy, Delete for everyone and Select messages.</p><p><b>9. Watch your numbers.</b> Open the <a class="dl" href="/shop#go-dashboard">Product Dashboard</a> or the <a class="dl" href="/shop#go-advdash">Advanced Dashboard</a>. On any card tap the three dots to switch the time range.</p><p><b>10. Share your shop.</b> Tap <a class="dl" href="/shop#go-shoplink">My shop link</a> to copy it and paste it anywhere. Your visitors see your shop; only you see your private numbers.</p><p><b>11. Language and help.</b> Change the language in <a class="dl" href="/shop#go-language">Language</a>. Use <a class="dl" href="/shop#go-help">Help</a> or the <a class="dl" href="/shop#go-ai">AI Assistant</a> if you cannot find something. Open the three-line menu at the top left for all options in one place.</p></section>
<section id="s22"><div class="num">22</div><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><p><b>Do you sell my information?</b> No.</p><p><b>Who can see my payment QR?</b> Only a buyer who chooses online payment for that product. It is not shown on your public shop page.</p><p><b>Can a buyer see my gateway secret?</b> No. Nobody can see it, including you after you save it. If you lose track of it, disconnect and connect again with new keys from your Razorpay dashboard.</p><p><b>What if I pay less than the price?</b> The order is not confirmed. A seller or operator checks the amount received, and for gateway payments our server checks it automatically. Paying more than the price still confirms the order, but you should pay the exact amount.</p><p><b>What if my gateway payment was deducted but the order shows pending?</b> Wait a few minutes and check <a class="dl" href="/shop#go-orders">My orders</a>. If money was deducted for a payment that failed, the bank or gateway normally returns it. Contact us through <a class="dl" href="/shop#go-help">Help</a> with your order number if it does not.</p><p><b>Why was my listing rejected?</b> The most common reasons are an expired date, a QR image that cannot be scanned, or photos that do not show the product. Fix the listing and post it again.</p><p><b>Can I delete a message I sent by mistake?</b> Yes. Press and hold it and choose Delete for everyone. It disappears for the other person too.</p><p><b>Can I delete the grey &ldquo;This message was deleted&rdquo; notices?</b> Yes. Press and hold one, tick as many as you like, and tap the dustbin.</p><p><b>Can I send videos?</b> No. Only photos can be sent in chat.</p><p><b>Does the other person know when I have read their message?</b> Yes. Two green ticks appear on their message once you open the chat.</p><p><b>Who pays for delivery?</b> For now the seller delivers and pays the delivery cost. After Stratic Market has been installed on your phone for six months, Stratic Market pays the delivery cost.</p><p><b>Is there a commission?</b> Not at present. See the Fees section.</p><p><b>How do I stop sounds in chat?</b> Open the three-dot menu in a chat and switch Sound off.</p><p><b>How do I change the chat theme?</b> Open the three-dot menu in a chat and choose Chat theme. You can pick Royal Gold, Midnight, Emerald, Rose or Ivory.</p><p><b>How do I see who viewed my products?</b> Open your shop link while signed in. The viewer list with names and photos appears near the top. People who were not signed in are counted but not named.</p><p><b>How do I list a product in another currency?</b> Choose the currency in the last field of the listing form before you post.</p><p><b>How do I close my account?</b> Use <a class="dl" href="/shop#go-help">Help</a> and ask us to close it. We will delete or anonymise your information as described in this Policy.</p><p><b>I think my account was used by someone else.</b> Change your password immediately, sign out on all shared devices, and tell us through <a class="dl" href="/shop#go-help">Help</a>.</p></section>
<section id="s23"><div class="num">23</div><h2>Contact us</h2><p>If you have a question about this Policy or about your information, open <a class="dl" href="/shop#go-help">Help</a> in the app or ask the <a class="dl" href="/shop#go-ai">AI Assistant</a> to guide you. Please include your account email and, where relevant, the order number, so that we can help you faster.</p></section>
